<article class="env-remark" id="02WH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02WH">Remark <span data-tag="02WH">65.4.3</span>.</a> Of the properties mentioned which are stable under base change (as listed in Remark <a href="/tag/02WF" data-tag="02WF">65.4.1</a>) the following are also <em>fpqc local on the base</em> (and a fortiori fppf local on the base): </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for immersions we have this for 
</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>
closed immersions, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L6" data-tag="02L6">35.23.21</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
open immersions, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L3" data-tag="02L3">35.23.18</a>, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
quasi-compact immersions, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L8" data-tag="02L8">35.23.23</a>, 
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li><li><p>
quasi-compact, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KQ" data-tag="02KQ">35.23.1</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally closed, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KS" data-tag="02KS">35.23.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(quasi-)separated, see Descent, Lemmas <a href="/tag/02KR" data-tag="02KR">35.23.2</a>, and <a href="/tag/02KU" data-tag="02KU">35.23.6</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
monomorphism, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02YK" data-tag="02YK">35.23.33</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
surjective, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KV" data-tag="02KV">35.23.7</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally injective, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KW" data-tag="02KW">35.23.10</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
affine, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L5" data-tag="02L5">35.23.20</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
quasi-affine, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L7" data-tag="02L7">35.23.22</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) of finite type, see Descent, Lemmas <a href="/tag/02KX" data-tag="02KX">35.23.12</a>, and <a href="/tag/02KZ" data-tag="02KZ">35.23.14</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) quasi-finite, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VI" data-tag="02VI">35.23.26</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) of finite presentation, see Descent, Lemmas <a href="/tag/02KY" data-tag="02KY">35.23.13</a>, and <a href="/tag/02L0" data-tag="02L0">35.23.15</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
locally of finite type of relative dimension $d$, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VJ" data-tag="02VJ">35.23.27</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally open, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KT" data-tag="02KT">35.23.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
flat, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L2" data-tag="02L2">35.23.17</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
syntomic, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VK" data-tag="02VK">35.23.28</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
smooth, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VL" data-tag="02VL">35.23.29</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
unramified (resp. G-unramified), see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VM" data-tag="02VM">35.23.30</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
étale, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VN" data-tag="02VN">35.23.31</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
proper, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L1" data-tag="02L1">35.23.16</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
finite or integral, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02LA" data-tag="02LA">35.23.25</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
finite locally free, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VO" data-tag="02VO">35.23.32</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally submersive, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CEW" data-tag="0CEW">35.23.5</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universal homeomorphism, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CEX" data-tag="0CEX">35.23.11</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Note that the property of being an “immersion” may not be fpqc local on the base, but in Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02YM" data-tag="02YM">35.24.1</a> we proved that it is fppf local on the base. </p>
